IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- aia-scope: Articles 1 and 2 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by
-- Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): subject matter and scope.
-- READ-ONLY for the parts. A seat asks "does the Regulation apply to me, to this system, to this activity?" by calling the paragraph
-- functions below and combining their answers with `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs`.
--
-- Article 1 (purpose; what the Regulation lays down) creates no rule and is not encoded (coverage row: inert, reason 1).
--
-- How to read a result. Every paragraph function takes `the date asked` first and returns MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   NOTHING   not covered. Either Chapter I has not begun to apply (it applies from 2 February 2025: Art 113 third paragraph point (a)),
--             or the paragraph does not speak to these facts. A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--   JUST TRUE the paragraph says the Regulation applies (Art 2(1): "applies to").
--   JUST FALSE the paragraph says the Regulation does not apply, or does not affect a thing, in its own words
--             (a flat negative: "does not apply", "shall not affect", "applies neither ... nor").
-- The paragraph functions are NOT mutually exclusive; the combinator below puts the exclusions first, because paragraphs 3, 4, 6, 8, 10
-- and 12 say "does not apply" of things that paragraph 1 would otherwise reach (fork F-2-order: the text states no order).

§ `Has Chapter I begun to apply? (Art 113 third paragraph, point (a): Chapters I and II from 2 February 2025)`

-- Chapter I (Articles 1 to 4a) has no date of its own beyond point (a) of Article 113. The question is asked of no AI system.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

§ `Article 2(1): to whom the Regulation applies (a list that does not close, so a party outside it is "not covered")`

-- src:33 | (a) providers placing on the market or putting into service AI systems or placing on the market general-purpose AI models in the Union, irrespective of whether those providers are established or located within the Union or in a third country;
@ref Art 2(1)(a) (src:33)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party places an AI system on the market or puts it into service in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party places a general-purpose AI model on the market in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(a) the Regulation applies to the provider` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the party is a provider` AND (`the party places an AI system on the market or puts it into service in the Union` OR `the party places a general-purpose AI model on the market in the Union`)
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "irrespective of whether those providers are established or located within the Union or in a third country": the place is not asked
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): Art 2(1) names who the Regulation applies to without saying it applies to no one else

-- src:34 | (b) deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located within the Union;
@ref Art 2(1)(b) (src:34)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a deployer of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party's place` IS A `Place of a party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(b) the Regulation applies to the deployer in the Union` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the party is a deployer of an AI system` AND `the party's place` EQUALS `Established or located in the Union`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): see limb (c) for a deployer in a third country

-- src:35 | (c) providers and deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located in a third country, where the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union;
@ref Art 2(1)(c) (src:35)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a provider or a deployer of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party's place` IS A `Place of a party`
      `the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(c) the Regulation applies to the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the party is a provider or a deployer of an AI system`
              AND `the party's place` EQUALS `Established or located in a third country`
              AND `the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union"; list not closed

-- src:36 | (d) importers and distributors of AI systems;
@ref Art 2(1)(d) (src:36)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is an importer of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a distributor of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(d) the Regulation applies to the importer or distributor` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the party is an importer of AI systems` OR `the party is a distributor of AI systems`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)

-- src:37 | (e) product manufacturers placing on the market or putting into service an AI system together with their product and under their own name or trademark;
@ref Art 2(1)(e) (src:37)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a product manufacturer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it places an AI system on the market or puts it into service together with its product` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so under its own name or trademark` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(e) the Regulation applies to the product manufacturer` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the party is a product manufacturer`
              AND `it places an AI system on the market or puts it into service together with its product`
              AND `it does so under its own name or trademark`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "together with their product and under their own name or trademark"; list not closed

-- src:38 | (f) authorised representatives of providers, which are not established in the Union;
@ref Art 2(1)(f) (src:38)
-- fork F-2-1-f: "authorised representatives of providers, which are not established in the Union". Read as: the relative clause
-- describes the providers (Art 3(5) makes every authorised representative one located or established in the Union, so the
-- clause cannot describe the representatives). The other reading would apply the limb to representatives not established in the Union, which Art 3(5) rules out.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is an authorised representative of a provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider it represents is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(f) the Regulation applies to the authorised representative of a provider not established in the Union` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the party is an authorised representative of a provider` AND (NOT `the provider it represents is established in the Union`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "providers, which are not established in the Union"; list not closed

-- src:39 | (g) affected persons that are located in the Union.
@ref Art 2(1)(g) (src:39)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the person is an affected person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's place` IS A `Place of a party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1)(g) the Regulation applies to the affected person in the Union` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the person is an affected person` AND `the person's place` EQUALS `Established or located in the Union`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "affected persons that are located in the Union"; list not closed

§ `Article 2(2): high-risk systems under Article 6(1) with Section B products (replaced by the Omnibus)`

-- src:41 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply. Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply. Article 57 applies only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
@ref Art 2(2) (src:41) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420)
-- Reads the list as closed by "only": a provision not in it does not apply to such a system (JUST FALSE). The conditional provisions (Article 57
-- as enacted; Articles 57, 58 and 59 as amended) apply "only in so far as" the requirements have been integrated in the Union harmonisation legislation.
-- A reference to the whole of Article 6 is mixed (only paragraph 1 applies): NOTHING. The letter of an Article is "" or "a": Article 60a is number 60, letter "a".
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A `Article reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF NOT (`the route to high-risk` EQUALS `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` AND `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by ... Section B of Annex I"
         ELSE IF `the provision`'s number EQUALS 6 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "" AND `the provision`'s paragraph EQUALS 0
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only paragraph 1 of Article 6 is named; a reference to the whole Article is mixed
              ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
                   WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as enacted: Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109, Article 112; Article 57 if integrated
                       IF       (`the provision`'s number EQUALS 6 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "" AND `the provision`'s paragraph EQUALS 1)
                             OR (`the provision`'s number AT LEAST 102 AND `the provision`'s number AT MOST 109 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "")
                             OR (`the provision`'s number EQUALS 112 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "")
                       THEN JUST TRUE
                       ELSE IF `the provision`'s number EQUALS 57 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS ""
                            THEN JUST `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Article 57 applies only in so far as the requirements ... have been integrated"
                            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"
                   WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as amended: Article 6(1), Article 60a, Articles 102 to 112; Articles 57, 58, 59 if integrated
                       IF       (`the provision`'s number EQUALS 6 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "" AND `the provision`'s paragraph EQUALS 1)
                             OR (`the provision`'s number EQUALS 60 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "a")
                             OR (`the provision`'s number AT LEAST 102 AND `the provision`'s number AT MOST 112 AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS "")
                       THEN JUST TRUE
                       ELSE IF (`the provision`'s number EQUALS 57 OR `the provision`'s number EQUALS 58 OR `the provision`'s number EQUALS 59) AND `the provision`'s letter EQUALS ""
                            THEN JUST `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as the requirements ... have been integrated"
                            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply"

§ `Article 2(3) to (6): areas the Regulation does not apply to`

-- src:43 | 3. This Regulation does not apply to areas outside the scope of Union law, and shall not, in any event, affect the competences of the Member States concerning national security, regardless of the type of entity entrusted by the Member States with carrying out tasks in relation to those competences.
@ref Art 2(3) first subparagraph (src:43)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter is an area outside the scope of Union law, or a competence of the Member States concerning national security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the matter outside the scope of Union law` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the matter is an area outside the scope of Union law, or a competence of the Member States concerning national security`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to areas outside the scope of Union law, and shall not, in any event, affect the competences of the Member States concerning national security"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the exclusion says nothing of other matters

-- src:44 | This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used with or without modification exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities.
@ref Art 2(3) second subparagraph (src:44)
-- "where and in so far": a system used for military, defence or national security purposes only in part is excluded only in that part, so
-- the input is TRUE only where the whole of the placing, putting into service or use is exclusively for those purposes.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is placed on the market, put into service or used, with or without modification, exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the AI system is placed on the market, put into service or used, with or without modification, exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used ... exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "exclusively"; a system with any other use is outside the exclusion

-- src:45 | This Regulation does not apply to AI systems which are not placed on the market or put into service in the Union, where the output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities.
@ref Art 2(3) third subparagraph (src:45)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is not placed on the market or put into service in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the AI system is not placed on the market or put into service in the Union` AND `its output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to AI systems which are not placed on the market or put into service in the Union, where the output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the output is used in the Union exclusively for ..."

-- src:46 | 4. This Regulation applies neither to public authorities in a third country nor to international organisations falling within the scope of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1, where those authorities or organisations use AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States, provided that such a third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals.
@ref Art 2(4) (src:46)
-- "provided that ... provides adequate safeguards": where the safeguards are missing the exclusion does not operate; the paragraph then says nothing.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a public authority in a third country or an international organisation falling within the scope of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it uses AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(4) the Regulation applies to the third-country public authority or international organisation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the party is a public authority in a third country or an international organisation falling within the scope of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1`
              AND `it uses AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States`
              AND `the third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation applies neither to public authorities in a third country nor to international organisations ... provided that such a third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where those authorities ... use AI systems in the framework of ..."; "provided that" the safeguards are adequate

-- src:47 | 5. This Regulation shall not affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services as set out in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.
@ref Art 2(5) (src:47)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provision is a provision on the liability of providers of intermediary services as set out in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(5) the Regulation affects the application of the provision on the liability of providers of intermediary services` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the provision is a provision on the liability of providers of intermediary services as set out in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation shall not affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services as set out in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks of those provisions only

-- src:48 | 6. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development.
@ref Art 2(6) (src:48)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the thing is an AI system or an AI model, including its output` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was specifically developed and put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was so developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(6) the Regulation applies to the AI system or model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the thing is an AI system or an AI model, including its output`
              AND `it was specifically developed and put into service`
              AND `it was so developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the sole purpose of scientific research and development"

§ `Article 2(7): personal-data law (replaced by the Omnibus: the "without prejudice" provisions changed)`

-- src:50 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Without prejudice to Articles 4a and 59 of this Regulation, this Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. This Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680, without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59 of this Regulation.
@ref Art 2(7) (src:50) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427)
-- First sentence, both texts: Union data protection law applies to the personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations of this Regulation.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `personal data is processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7) Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to the personal data` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `personal data is processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation"

-- src:50 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Without prejudice to Articles 4a and 59 of this Regulation, this Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. This Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680, without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59 of this Regulation.
@ref Art 2(7) (src:50) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427)
-- Second sentence. The provisions the Regulation reserves ("without prejudice to") may affect the four instruments, so for them the sentence says nothing.
-- VERSION as enacted: Article 10(5) and Article 59. VERSION as amended: Articles 4a and 59. Article 4a is number 4, letter "a".
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the instrument is Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, Directive 2002/58/EC or Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of this Regulation` IS A `Article reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7) the Regulation affects the data protection instrument through the provision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF NOT `the instrument is Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, Directive 2002/58/EC or Directive (EU) 2016/680`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names those four instruments
         ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
              WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                       -- VERSION as enacted
                  IF (`the provision of this Regulation`'s number EQUALS 10 AND `the provision of this Regulation`'s paragraph EQUALS 5) OR (`the provision of this Regulation`'s number EQUALS 59 AND `the provision of this Regulation`'s letter EQUALS "")
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59"
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680"
              WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                       -- VERSION as amended
                  IF (`the provision of this Regulation`'s number EQUALS 4 AND `the provision of this Regulation`'s letter EQUALS "a") OR (`the provision of this Regulation`'s number EQUALS 59 AND `the provision of this Regulation`'s letter EQUALS "")
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without prejudice to Articles 4a and 59 of this Regulation"
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680"

§ `Article 2(8) to (12): research, other acts, personal use, workers, open-source`

-- src:52 | 8. This Regulation does not apply to any research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models prior to their being placed on the market or put into service. Such activities shall be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law. Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion.
@ref Art 2(8) (src:52)
-- Third sentence: "Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion": for it the exclusion does not operate and the paragraph says nothing more.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prior to their being placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is testing in real world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8) the Regulation applies to the research, testing or development activity` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models`
              AND `it is prior to their being placed on the market or put into service`
              AND (NOT `it is testing in real world conditions`)
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to any research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models prior to their being placed on the market or put into service"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prior to their being placed on the market"; "Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion"

@ref Art 2(8)
-- Second sentence: "Such activities shall be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law." A "shall" with no time limit and no stated consequence: no breach path (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prior to their being placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is testing in real world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8) the activity must be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models`
              AND `it is prior to their being placed on the market or put into service`
              AND (NOT `it is testing in real world conditions`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such activities" are the excluded ones

-- src:53 | 9. This Regulation is without prejudice to the rules laid down by other Union legal acts related to consumer protection and product safety.
@ref Art 2(9) (src:53)
