    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the legal act is another Union legal act related to consumer protection or product safety`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation is without prejudice to the rules laid down by other Union legal acts related to consumer protection and product safety"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of acts on consumer protection and product safety

-- src:54 | 10. This Regulation does not apply to obligations of deployers who are natural persons using AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity.
