`Art 2(11) the Regulation precludes the more favourable law or collective agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the law, regulation, administrative provision or collective agreement is more favourable to workers in terms of protecting their rights in respect of the use of AI systems by employers`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not preclude the Union or Member States from maintaining or introducing laws, regulations or administrative provisions which are more favourable to workers ..., or from encouraging or allowing the application of collective agreements which are more favourable to workers"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of provisions "more favourable to workers"

-- src:56 | 12. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems released under free and open-source licences, unless they are placed on the market or put into service as high-risk AI systems or as an AI system that falls under Article 5 or 50.
@ref Art 2(12) (src:56)
-- The "unless" limb takes three facts from other parts of the Regulation: the classification as high-risk (Article 6), and whether the system falls under Article 5 or Article 50. They are inputs here.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is placed on the market or put into service as a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it falls under Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it falls under Article 50` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(12) the Regulation applies to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence`
              AND (NOT (`it is placed on the market or put into service as a high-risk AI system` OR `it falls under Article 5` OR `it falls under Article 50`))
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to AI systems released under free and open-source licences, unless ..."
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless they are placed on the market or put into service as high-risk AI systems or as an AI system that falls under Article 5 or 50"; the exclusion then does not operate

§ `Article 2(13): limiting the requirements for Article 6(1) systems (inserted by the Omnibus)`

-- src:58 | 13. For high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(1), the application of specific requirements or obligations laid down in Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25 may be limited, where and to the extent that:
-- src:59 | (a) Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned; and
-- src:60 | (b) such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation.
-- src:61 | By 2 August 2027, the Commission shall adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to supplement this Regulation by specifying the high-risk AI systems concerned, the requirements or obligations that may be limited, the conditions under which such limitation applies, and the scope of the limitation.
@ref Art 2(13) (src:58-61)
-- A "may" gated by "where and to the extent that": the answer when a condition fails is JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)).
-- The other reading is NOTHING (a grant limited by its own wording): fork F-2-13, split site (ii). "To the extent" is a matter of degree the function does not measure.
-- Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25 are numbers 9 to 15 and 17 to 25 with letter "".
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the requirement or obligation` IS A `Article reference`
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(13) the application of the requirement or obligation may be limited` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 13 is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN         -- VERSION as amended
             IF NOT (`the route to high-risk` EQUALS `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I`)
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(1)"
             ELSE IF NOT (       `the requirement or obligation`'s letter EQUALS ""
                          AND (   (`the requirement or obligation`'s number AT LEAST 9 AND `the requirement or obligation`'s number AT MOST 15)
                               OR (`the requirement or obligation`'s number AT LEAST 17 AND `the requirement or obligation`'s number AT MOST 25)))
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25"
                  ELSE IF       `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
                            AND `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`
                       THEN JUST TRUE
                       ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be limited, where and to the extent that: (a) ...; and (b) ..."; both conditions are needed (split site (ii))

-- The delegated acts: "By 2 August 2027, the Commission shall adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 ...". The Commission is not a seat;
-- the rule is encoded for what it decides (the date) and as a regulative rule, so that the missed deadline reaches BREACH.
@ref Art 2(13)
`Art 2(13) the date by which the Commission is to adopt the delegated acts` MEANS Date 2 8 2027

DECLARE `Art 2(13) body` IS ONE OF
    Commission

DECLARE `Art 2(13) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 2(13) adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 specifying the high-risk AI systems concerned, the requirements or obligations that may be limited, the conditions under which such limitation applies, and the scope of the limitation`

@ref Art 2(13)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 2(13) body` `Art 2(13) act`
`Art 2(13) the Commission's duty to adopt the delegated acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN FULFILLED  -- VERSION as enacted: paragraph 13 is not in the text; nothing is owed
    WHEN `as amended` THEN            -- VERSION as amended
        PARTY Commission
        MUST `Art 2(13) adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 specifying the high-risk AI systems concerned, the requirements or obligations that may be limited, the conditions under which such limitation applies, and the scope of the limitation`
        WITHIN (Day `Art 2(13) the date by which the Commission is to adopt the delegated acts`) MINUS (Day `Omnibus Art 4 the Omnibus enters into force`)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Commission BECAUSE "the delegated acts were not adopted by 2 August 2027 as Article 2(13) requires"

§ `Putting the paragraphs together`

-- The combinator. A seat collects the answers of the paragraphs that fit its facts, as a list, and asks what they add up to.
-- An exclusion that says "does not apply" (JUST FALSE) comes first; then an inclusion (JUST TRUE); otherwise NOTHING.
-- NOTHING is never turned into FALSE: with no paragraph that speaks, the answer is NOTHING (not covered).
GIVEN `the answers of the paragraphs` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers of the paragraphs`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): at least one of paragraphs 3 to 12 says the Regulation does not apply
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of the paragraphs`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no paragraph speaks to these facts
